# Vouch — Backend Agent Rules

Read `context/1-project-overview.md` through `context/7-units.md` before writing any code. Full detail lives there; this file is the always-loaded summary.

## Non-negotiable
* No BVN, NIN, bank details, loan logic, Squad calls, AI risk scores, or secrets, anywhere in backend code.
* No direct work on `main`. Work on `backend/trust-profile-api`. Open a PR into `rebuild/trust-profile-mvp`. Never merge it yourself.
* Migrations are additive only. Never modify an applied migration or delete production data.
* Every owner endpoint uses the existing Supabase JWT middleware and validates ownership.
* The public profile endpoint and the confirmation endpoints expose only deliberately public data: no email, no Supabase user ID, no confirmation token, no unconfirmed private evidence.
* Use only the approved status vocabulary: SELF_REPORTED / CUSTOMER_CONFIRMED, "self-reported," "customer-confirmed." Never imply a credit score, verified identity, or a guarantee of performance. See `context/3-ui-context.md`.
* Do not touch, refactor, or delete legacy loan/score/Ajo/Jobs/Squad/demo code. Leave it isolated.

## Working style
* One atomic unit at a time, from `context/7-units.md`, in order. Do not skip ahead or batch units.
* If a requirement conflicts with the context files or a detail is missing, stop and ask. Do not assume.
* Document every new endpoint, model, or migration in `backend/TRUST_PROFILE_API.md` as you build it.
* Before every push: `git diff --check`, `git status --short`, and the relevant build/test.

## Target
Vouch v0.1, October 1, 2026. See `context/1-project-overview.md` for the full release gate.
